                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:10",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And the land had rest forty years. And Othniel the son of Kenaz died.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:11",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And the children of Israel did evil again in the sight of the Lord: and the Lord strengthened Eglon the king of Moab against Israel, because they had done evil in the sight of the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:12",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And he gathered unto him the children of Ammon and Amalek, and went and smote Israel, and possessed the city of palm trees.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:13",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "So the children of Israel served Eglon the king of Moab eighteen years.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:14",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "But when the children of Israel cried unto the Lord, the Lord raised them up a deliverer, Ehud the son of Gera, a Benjamite, a man lefthanded: and by him the children of Israel sent a present unto Eglon the king of Moab.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:15",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "But Ehud made him a dagger which had two edges, of a cubit length; and he did gird it under his raiment upon his right thigh.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:16",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And he brought the present unto Eglon king of Moab: and Eglon was a very fat man.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 65
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:17",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And when he had made an end to offer the present, he sent away the people that bare the present.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:18",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "But he himself turned again from the quarries that were by Gilgal, and said, I have a secret errand unto thee, O king: who said, Keep silence. And all that stood by him went out from him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "OR message."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 55
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:19",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ehud came unto him; and he was sitting in a summer parlour, which he had for himself alone. And Ehud said, I have a message from God unto thee. And he arose out of his seat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 168,
            "end": 171
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:20",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ehud put forth his left hand, and took the dagger from his right thigh, and thrust it into his belly:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:21",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And the haft also went in after the blade; and the fat closed upon the blade, so that he could not draw the dagger out of his belly; and the dirt came out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "OR handle."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:22",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Ehud went forth through the porch, and shut the doors of the parlour upon him, and locked them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "HEB upper, or roof, chamber."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:23",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "When he was gone out, his servants came; and when they saw that, behold, the doors of the parlour were locked, they said, Surely he covereth his feet in his summer chamber.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 98,
            "end": 102
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:24",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And they tarried till they were ashamed: and, behold, he opened not the doors of the parlour; therefore they took a key, and opened them: and, behold, their lord was fallen down dead on the earth.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 137
          },
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 165
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:25",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And Ehud escaped while they tarried, and passed beyond the quarries, and escaped unto Seirath.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:26",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass, when he was come, that he blew a trumpet in the mountain of Ephraim, and the children of Israel went down with him from the mount, and he before them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:27",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "And he said unto them, Follow after me: for the Lord hath delivered your enemies the Moabites into your hand. And they went down after him, and took the fords of Jordan toward Moab, and suffered not a man to pass over.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:28",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "And they slew of Moab at that time about ten thousand men, all lusty, and all men of valour; and there escaped not a man.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 63,
            "end": 68,
            "text": "HEB fat or hardy."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Judges 3:29",
        "book": "Judges",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "So Moab was subdued that day under the hand of Israel. And the land had rest fourscore years.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 3,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "2 Kgs. 3:18."
          },
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 19,
            "text": "Ex. 14:30 (1–30); Judg. 10:11 (11–12)."
          },
          {
            "start": 77,
            "end": 86,
            "text": "OR eighty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Kgs. 3:18.",
            "prettyString": "2 Kings 3:18",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2kings",
